.TH "ODIR-DOT-DEFAULTS" "7" "" "odir 25.1.2+onesimus.0.2.0" "Onesimus Director Commands"
.SH NAME
odir\-dot\-defaults \- \&.defaults: Get default settings
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\&.defaults [job=<job>] [client=<client>] [storage=<storage>] [pool=<pool>]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Shows the main settings of a job, client, storage or pool as key=value lines. The WebUI and scripts use it to prefill forms such as run or restore with values from the configuration. It reads only the configuration and changes nothing.
.PP
Give exactly one resource per call; the name must match exactly. A JobDefs template is not a job and returns nothing, nor does a resource hidden by the console's ACL. For pool= one line reads purge_oldest_volume==0 with a double equals sign, as in Bareos. Under API 2 an error leaves result empty instead of an empty defaults object.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.SS "\&.defaults"
.TP
.B "job=<job>"
Job name (name; values from .jobs)
.TP
.B "client=<client>"
Client name (name; values from .clients)
.TP
.B "storage=<storage>"
Storage name (name; values from .storages)
.TP
.B "pool=<pool>"
Pool name (name; values from .pools)
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B "\&.defaults job=backup\-bareos\-fd"
show the defaults of a job
.TP
.B "\&.defaults pool=Full"
show the settings of pool Full
.SH ORIGIN
Bareos console command.
